# The circuit, in a bomber: take off, fly the pattern left-hand at circuit
# height, and land back on the runway you left.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The pattern is a jet's**, as Boeing's 737 Flight Crew Training Manual
# describes a visual circuit: about 1,500 ft above the runway, the downwind
# leg flown with the take-off flap out at its manoeuvring speed about two
# miles abeam, the gear down and more flap before the turn on to base, and
# the landing flap set before final. The stages are the light aircraft's -
# see light-aircraft-circuit.lesson for why each ends where it does.
#
# **The bands are measured, with room.** Flown by the AI pilot round a
# 1,500 ft circuit the B-2A climbs out at 251 knots, 21 over its climbing
# speed; holds 1,487 to 1,500 ft downwind; and flies final at vref-4 to
# vref+10. The downwind band is 150 ft either side, half as much again as
# the FAA's Airline Transport Pilot ACS allows (100 ft) and inside the 250 ft
# the fault is flown with.
# **Since 2026-09-26 final reaches 20 knots over**, as the bomber's approach
# lesson does and for the same reason: the B-2A cannot slow on the approach
# (a tail in docs/COMPLETION_PLAN.md). Until then it flew final in a Dutch
# roll, and the drag of its rudders working either way held it to vref+10;
# with the approach autopilot's yaw damper it comes down final level, at
# vref-4 to vref+14.

name The circuit in a bomber
teaches bomber

stage The take-off
do Take-off thrust, keep her straight on the centreline, and rotate at the rotation speed
do Gear up and climb away once she is off the ground
until position/h-agl-ft >= start+200

stage The climb out
do Climb away straight ahead, the take-off flap still out
do Do not turn until you are high enough
hold velocities/vc-kts climb-100 climb+200 Hold the climbing speed in the climb out
hold lesson/turned-deg -25 25 Keep her straight until you are high enough to turn
until position/h-agl-ft >= start+400

stage The crosswind turn
do Turn left on to crosswind, still climbing
until lesson/turned-deg <= -80

stage Crosswind, and the turn on to downwind
do Climb on to circuit height and level off there
do Turn left on to downwind, about two miles abeam the runway
until lesson/turned-deg <= -80

stage Downwind
do Fly the downwind leg at circuit height, parallel to the runway, the take-off flap out
do Hold the height and the speed: the landing checks are done along here
hold position/h-agl-ft start-150 start+150 Hold the circuit height downwind
need lesson/flown-nm >= 1.0 Fly a downwind leg long enough to do the checks and settle
until lesson/turned-deg <= -50

stage Base, and the turn on to final
do Gear down and more flap, power back, turn left on to base and start down
do Landing flap, and turn left on to final to line up with the runway
until lesson/turned-deg <= -110

stage Final
do Hold the approach speed down to the threshold
hold velocities/vc-kts vref-10 vref+20 Hold the approach speed on final
until position/h-agl-ft <= 40

stage The landing
do Close the throttles over the threshold and flare
do Let her settle on the main wheels, and keep her straight on the roll
need gear/wow >= 0.5 Land her on the runway
until velocities/vg-fps <= 1.0
